{"duration_api_ms": 138116, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "fab97ffc-d7ef-494d-b171-0a7aa4713c81", "total_cost_usd": 0.3110882, "usage": {"input_tokens": 16, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 36271, "cache_read_input_tokens": 245261, "output_tokens": 11692, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 6366}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 36271, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7297, "cache_read_input_tokens": 49603, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3036, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3036}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-sonnet-5": {"inputTokens": 16, "outputTokens": 11692, "cacheReadInputTokens": 245261, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 36271, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.3110882, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 64000, "thinkingTokens": 6366, "canonicalModel": "claude-sonnet-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 26, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I've read through the repo and SPEC.md. Here's what an implementer needs to know before touching the five commands.\n\n## How the three exports differ\n\n| | System A (Ardent) | System B (Borough) | System C (Calder) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Shape | `#`-comment preamble, header, rows | header, rows | banner line, header, rows, `== N rows ==` trailer |\n| id / date / account / desc / amount cols | `entry_id, posted_on, account, memo, amount, currency` | `sys, doc_no, value_date, acct, descr, amount, cur` | `ref, txn_date, ledger_acct, narrative, gross_amount, ccy` |\n| Date format | ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` | ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` | **day-first** `DD/MM/YYYY` — a comment in `system_c.py` flags this explicitly as a landmine (rows past the 12th silently land in the wrong month if read month-first) |\n| Amount encoding | decimal dollars, 2dp, signed | **integer cents** (no decimal point) — `system_b.to_major_units` already exists and does this conversion; nothing else does | decimal dollars, 2dp, signed |\n| Quoting | quoted memo fields, `\"\"`-doubled internal quotes (real CSV quoting) | never quoted (descr is pre-scrubbed of delimiters) | never quoted |\n\n## Bugs/gaps you'll hit while implementing, not after\n\n- **`system_a.read_rows` currently *raises* on any quoted field**, but the sample file's very first data row (`A-10001`) has a quoted, comma-containing, `\"\"`-escaped memo. Since ingest must emit *every* posting, this reader needs fixing to actually parse quoted fields — `ledgerkit/core/fields.py`'s `split_record` already does exactly this (its doctest is the same string as the A-10001 line), so it's a drop-in fix. The existing test (`test_system_a_reads_an_export_without_quoted_memos`) only covers the unquoted case, so it won't break.\n- **`mapping.py`: account code `5200` is listed twice** in `ACCOUNT_NAMES` — the dict literal keeps the second entry, \"Contract Labor\", not \"Warehouse Labor\" from the docstring table. The docstring is stale; the dict is authoritative.\n- **`normalize()` drops refunds by default** (`keep_refunds=False`). `ingest` must call it with `keep_refunds=True` since SPEC requires every posting to appear — nothing is filtered at ingest time. `report`'s `--include-refunds` and `reconcile`'s \"refunds always included\" are then applied by reading back the already-complete normalized CSV, not by touching `normalize()`'s flag again.\n- **The existing readers raise on the first malformed row** (`strict=True` zip, immediate `LedgerParseError`). SPEC's `validate` needs to check *every* row and keep going after a bad one — so `validate` can't just call `system_x.read_rows()` and catch one exception; it needs its own permissive, per-row loop (still using each system's own line-splitting/date/amount rules) that logs a `WARNING` per rejected row and keeps checking the rest.\n- **`--config PATH` must work through the environment**, not a function argument. `load_settings()` deliberately takes no parameters (per CONVENTIONS) and reads `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` from `os.environ`. The global `--config` flag has to set that env var before calling `load_settings()`.\n- **Reconcile's per-line amounts are always 2dp**, independent of the `[report] decimals` setting — that setting only affects `report`'s totals.\n- **Rounding**: `Settings.format_amount` deliberately does *not* round — its docstring says so. The caller must `Decimal.quantize(..., rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)` once at display time before formatting; summing/grouping must stay unrounded Decimal until then.\n\n## Reusable pieces already in place\n`core/records.py` gives `Record`, `RECORD_COLUMNS`, `sort_key` (date, system, id — matches `ingest`'s required ordering) and `to_row()` (already formats amount to 2dp). `core/normalize.py` does the strip/upper/whitespace-collapse cleanup. `config.py`'s `DEFAULTS`/`Settings` already expose `decimals`, `unknown_account_label`, `tolerance`, `account_code_pattern`. None of the four new commands are wired into `build_parser()` yet — only `version`/`inspect` exist there today.\n\n## House rules to hold to\nNo `print` outside `cli.emit`; every new public function fully type-annotated; never touch `config/`; log via `ledgerkit.log.get_logger`; stdlib only; don't import `utils.cache` (it's for speed on large files but isn't part of the spec, and skipping it keeps this session's work simple/testable) or `legacy_parser`; flag names exactly `--out`, `--by`, `--records`, `--include-refunds`, `--tolerance`, `--config`.\n\nLet me know when you'd like me to start implementing — I'd suggest tackling them in the order `ingest` → `report`/`reconcile` (both read the normalized format) → `validate`, since `validate`'s permissive per-row logic is the most work and benefits from the per-system parsing rules being fresh.", "ttft_ms": 1344, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 138780, "uuid": "529613e2-1e16-4caf-96ad-f0329908abd2", "ttft_stream_ms": 837, "time_to_request_ms": 151, "first_content_frame_ms": 1020, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 140.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "sonnet", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/P/sonnet/topic-r3-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
