a new `ledgerkit/core/io.py`). Fixed a real bug along the way: `system_a.py`'s reader used to raise on any quoted memo field; it now uses the existing quote-aware `fields.split_record`, so quoted descriptions (like the sample's `A-10001`) are preserved instead of crashing the whole ingest.\n- **`report --by account|month`** — totals from the normalized file (`ledgerkit/report.py`), rounded once with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` at the configured `decimals`. Per your correction: fields are semicolon-separated, and refunds are included by default; `--include-refunds` is still accepted (for scripts that already pass it) but is now a no-op since inclusion is the default — flagged this decision so you can tell me if `--include-refunds` should instead do something else.\n- **`reconcile`** — groups by account/month/system, reports spreads over tolerance (`ledgerkit/reconcile.py`), `--tolerance` parsed straight to `Decimal`.\n- **`validate`** — checks every row of a file (doesn't stop at the first bad one) against the four SPEC rules, logging one `WARNING` per rejected row; added tolerant `iter_data_lines`/`read_header` helpers to each parser module for this, plus a `Calder read_header` that didn't exist before.\n- **`--config PATH`** — global option; sets `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` in the environment before `load_settings()` runs, matching the env-var-only contract in `config.py`. Never touches `config/`.\n\nVerified by hand against the sample files: `ingest` produced all 120 rows (42+39+39) including the quoted memo and correct day-first Calder dates; `reconcile`'s first mismatch line matched SPEC's worked example verbatim; `report`'s rounding matched CONVENTIONS' half-to-even table exactly; `validate` correctly flagged bad-date/bad-amount/bad-account-code/field-count-mismatch rows without stopping early, and reported \"cannot read file\" + exit 2 for a missing file.", "ttft_ms": 260804, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 463735, "uuid": "ea4b8dd9-ff19-483c-9185-a50a62ccb8ac", "ttft_stream_ms